In PowerShell:

powershell
scp "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\CP-0086.py" a5:/home/yaolu/
scp -r "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\save_path" a5:/home/yaolu/

Then on the A5:

bash
cd /home/yaolu
ls -la CP-0086.py
ls -R save_path | head -30

Then set up a clean environment. Important: your PATH currently has your own mr-3236 build in front, and reproducing a ticket against the daily package means using the daily package:

bash
source /home/yaolu/env.sh
which bishengir-compile
bishengir-compile --version
uptime

Confirm that's /data/ci_env/daily/pkg/... and not /home/yaolu/pkg/bin. Otherwise you'd be testing your patched compiler, not the build the ticket is about.

Then run it:

bash
cd /home/yaolu
python CP-0086.py 2>&1 | tee ~/CP-0086-repro.log
tail -40 ~/CP-0086-repro.log
